<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb nickel imports down 11.8 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb nickel imports down 11.8 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined nickel imports fell 11.8 percent to 4,259 tonnes in February from 4,827 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Feb 97    Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p> Total	   4,259     6,795	4,827</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Russia	    953     1,206	  913</p>
<p> S. Africa	 340	 978	  525</p>
<p> Zimbabwe	  774     1,118	  641</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first two months of 1997 totalled 11,054 tonnes, up 6.4 percent from 10,385 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
